From 01a7f0de5f7d6b65d9f11e2b6fbc5bbaef8e77be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Braden <snufflyy@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:19:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cellGcmSys: no drain-side ring recycle when the runtime's
 callback owns the ring

The drain recycles a title's ring when `current` reaches `end` and the
title's buffer-full callback will not. When the context still has the
runtime's own callback (cellGcmSetupContext installs it), current == end
is a normal state: the title calls that callback from gcmReserve next,
and it recycles. Recycling from the drain thread as well raced it: the
JUMP went over the title's last word at end-4 and `current` went back to
begin before the callback ran. Supersonic Acrobatic Rocket-Powered
Battle-Cars 01.09 keeps the runtime callback and sometimes never
submitted again after such a recycle (stuck on its loading screen).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/video/cellGcmSys.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
index 98a7fe3..0e6ea93 100644
--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -2499,6 +2499,16 @@ static void gcm_rsx_process_fifo_unlocked(void)
          * overruns first, so the first overrun is recycled by the path above
          * and near-end recycling is enabled from then on. */
         static int s_title_overran = 0;
+        /* The runtime's own buffer-full callback (cellGcmSetupContext installs
+         * it) does recycle: the title calls it from gcmReserve once `current`
+         * is at `end`, which is a normal state, not an overrun. Recycling here
+         * as well raced it from the drain thread: the JUMP went over the
+         * title's last word at end-4, `current` went back to begin before the
+         * title's callback ran (which then found nothing to recycle), and
+         * Supersonic Acrobatic Rocket-Powered Battle-Cars 01.09 (whose context
+         * keeps the runtime callback) sometimes never submitted again. */
+        const u32 cb_opd = ctx ? vm_read32(ctx + 0xC) : 0;
+        if (cb_opd && vm_read32(cb_opd) == GCM_FIFO_CALLBACK_SENTINEL_EA) begin = 0;
         if (begin && end > begin && cur >= end) {
             if (!s_title_overran)
                 fprintf(stderr, "[cellGcmSys] title overran its ring: ctx=0x%08X begin=0x%08X "
-- 
